{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123713","id":4604081150,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEmyz_g","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123713","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123713.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123713.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123713","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123713/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123713/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123713/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/1b9daea38254d0f67879a3a5c4aece955dc760b3","number":123713,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"LightmapGI: Keep the geometric side of a hit for unocclude and bounces","user":{"login":"samjanny","id":3447762,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDc3NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3447762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny","html_url":"https://github.com/samjanny","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Description\n\n#99538 added transparency support to LightmapGI and made ray hits respect the material cull mode.\n\nAs part of that change, `trace_ray()` applies the material cull mode before returning whether a triangle was hit from the front or the back.\n\nFor `CULL_DISABLED` materials, this means every hit is reported as a front-face hit, so the geometric side of the triangle is lost.\n\nThis causes two problems during light baking:\n\n- The unocclude pass can no longer detect back faces around texels located inside geometry.\n- Indirect bounce rays that hit the inside of opaque double-sided geometry shade the outer side of the face instead. This can let buried texels and geometric junctions collect light from outside the volume.\n\nThis change keeps `trace_ray()` geometric and applies the material cull mode only in the callers that need the material-facing side.\n\nAs a result:\n\n- unocclude can use the true geometric front/back side;\n- shadow rays keep their existing cull and transparency behavior;\n- transmission paths remain unchanged;\n- transparent bounce paths remain unchanged;\n- opaque back faces made visible by the material cull mode are shaded from the side the ray actually hit.\n\nFor those opaque back-face hits, the normal is flipped toward the ray, matching the renderer's back-facing fragment behavior. The direct-light texture is not sampled for that case because it contains lighting for the front side only.\n\nThis is not a revert of #99538. The transparency and cull-mode behavior introduced there is preserved.\n\n## Testing\n\nA synthetic LightmapGI regression suite was used before and after the change.\n\nTest cases include:\n\n- opaque `CULL_BACK` geometry;\n- opaque double-sided geometry;\n- thin double-sided opaque planes;\n- transparent glass;\n- colored transparent glass;\n- alpha/cutout surfaces;\n- double-sided alpha surfaces;\n- two transparent surfaces in sequence.\n\nResults:\n\n- Opaque `CULL_BACK` control scenes are unchanged where expected.\n- Transparent glass output is bit-identical to master.\n- Colored transparent glass output is bit-identical to master.\n- Two transparent surfaces in sequence are bit-identical to master.\n- Alpha/cutout transmission through transparent regions is preserved.\n- Invalid lighting inside opaque double-sided geometry is strongly reduced.\n\nOn the real-world regression scene, using raw lightmap output with the denoiser disabled:\n\n- 347 / 357 buried texels that were black in Godot 4.3 recover at least 80% toward the 4.3 result.\n- The previous diagnostic 4.3-style variant recovered 348 / 357, but also changed modern transparency behavior.\n- The new fix preserves the modern transparent path while recovering essentially the same opaque-geometry cases.\n\nA diagnostic build that changed only unocclude was also tested and did not fix the main leakage, confirming that the bounce-side handling is required as well.\n\n## Notes\n\nThin double-sided geometry remains an edge case for the unocclude heuristic because it cannot inherently distinguish a thin plane from the inside surface of a closed volume.\n\nThis PR intentionally preserves the current transparent path rather than restoring the pre-4.4 behavior.\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T15:50:13Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T09:14:27Z","closed_at":"2026-09-23T08:57:27Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b265f50e36d98259757c588ce9a24ec1f8e62ebe","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"samjanny:fix-lightmap-backface-unocclude","ref":"fix-lightmap-backface-unocclude","repo":null,"sha":"1b9daea38254d0f67879a3a5c4aece955dc760b3","user":{"login":"samjanny","id":3447762,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDc3NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3447762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny","html_url":"https://github.com/samjanny","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},"base":{"label":"godotengine:master","ref":"master","repo":{"id":15634981,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxNTYzNDk4MQ==","name":"godot","full_name":"godotengine/godot","owner":{"login":"godotengine","id":6318500,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjYzMTg1MDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6318500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/godotengine","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users